    "A second cause is poor urban planning. Jobs, schools and shops are frequently located far from residential areas, which forces people to travel long distances every day. To tackle this problem, local authorities should encourage mixed-use developments so that people can live close to where they work. In addition, charging drivers a fee to enter the city centre would discourage unnecessary trips. The money raised could then be used to improve cycling lanes and pavements.",
