    "label": "C",
    "text": "Keeping bees is a skilled job. A beekeeper looks after boxes called hives, each of which may hold fifty thousand insects. In spring, the beekeeper checks that the queen is laying eggs and that the workers have enough space. In summer, extra honey is collected, and some hives are even driven to farms where fruit trees are flowering. Beekeepers wear light protective clothing and move slowly, because quick movements can make the bees nervous. Many say the work teaches patience, and the honey is a pleasant reward."
